--TEST--
`Core\Markdown\Live` returns empty HTML for `finish()` with nothing pushed and for an empty piece, cleans a raw HTML block, writes footnotes at `finish()`, and ends the document when a function throws an error — `rule:core-classes/markdown-chunks`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Markdown::live, Core\Markdown\Live::push, Core\Markdown\Live::finish, Core\Markdown\Update::done, Core\Markdown\Update::open
class Guard
{
    // Throws an error for every link.
    public static function link(string $url): ?string
    {
        throw new RuntimeError("no links here");
    }
}

// `finish` with nothing pushed returns empty HTML.
Core\Markdown\Live $empty = Core\Markdown::live();
echo "empty: ", Core\Html::toSource($empty->finish(), "the case prints the rest"), "|\n";

// A push of an empty string finishes nothing and shows nothing.
Core\Markdown\Live $live = Core\Markdown::live();
Core\Markdown\Update $first = $live->push("");
echo "done: ", Core\Html::toSource($first->done(), "the case prints a part"), "|\n";
echo "open: ", Core\Html::toSource($first->open(), "the case prints a part"), "|\n";

// A raw HTML block is cleaned. The script is removed.
Core\Markdown\Update $second = $live->push("<div class=\"note\">\nSee the note.<script>alert(1)</script>\n</div>\n\n");
echo "done: ", Core\Html::toSource($second->done(), "the case prints a part"), "|\n";
echo "open: ", Core\Html::toSource($second->open(), "the case prints a part"), "|\n";

// The footnote is defined before its use. `finish` writes the footnote text at the end.
Core\Markdown\Update $third = $live->push("[^n]: The note.\n\nText[^n].\n");
echo "done: ", Core\Html::toSource($third->done(), "the case prints a part"), "|\n";
echo "finish: ", Core\Html::toSource($live->finish(), "the case prints the rest"), "|\n";

// A function that throws an error ends the document.
Core\Markdown\Live $broken = Core\Markdown::live(link: fn (string $url): ?string => Guard::link($url));
try {
    $broken->push("[a](/a)\n\nnext\n");
} catch (RuntimeError $failed) {
    echo $failed->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $broken->finish();
} catch (RuntimeError $ended) {
    echo $ended->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
empty: |
done: |
open: |
done: |
open: <div>
See the note.
</div>
|
done: <div>
See the note.
</div>
|
finish: <p>Text<sup><a href="#md-fn-1" id="md-fnref-1">1</a></sup>.</p>
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="md-fn-1">
<p>The note.</p>
 <a href="#md-fnref-1">↩</a></li>
</ol>
|
no links here
Core\Markdown\Live::finish(): this document has ended, because `finish()` was called or a callback threw an error. Create a new one with `Core\Markdown::live()`.
